sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    
    box rgb(240, 248, 255) User Space
    participant App as User App
    end
    
    box rgb(230, 240, 255) Linux Kernel Space
    participant VFS as VFS (File System)
    participant PCI as PCI Subsystem
    participant Driver as vGPU Driver (vGPU-Core)
    end
    
    box rgb(255, 245, 238) Motherboard
    participant RAM as System RAM (Host)
    participant PCIe as PCIe Bus (Root Complex)
    end
    
    box rgb(245, 255, 250) FPGA Hardware (Artix-7 XC7A200T)
    participant AXI_PCIe as AXI PCIe IP (axi_pcie_0)
    participant SmartConnect as AXI SmartConnect
    participant Regs as MMIO Regs (vgpu_axi_lite_regs)
    participant DMA as DMA Master Engine (vgpu_dma_master)
    participant Core as Compute Core ALU (vgpu_compute_core)
    end

    %% Phase 1: Boot & Driver Load
    Note over App, Core: [Phase 1] Boot & Driver Initialization
    PCI->>PCIe: PCIe Bus Enumeration (BIOS/Kernel boot)
    PCIe-->>PCI: Discover FPGA (Vendor ID: 0x10EE, Device ID: 0x7021)
    Note over PCI, PCIe: PCIe Configuration (BAR0 Sizing & Allocation: 64KB)
    PCI->>PCI: Assign Physical Address space for BAR0
    PCI->>AXI_PCIe: PCIe Config Write: Write Physical Addr back to BAR0
    
    Driver->>PCI: module_init() -> pci_register_driver()
    PCI->>Driver: Match ID -> vgpu_probe(pdev)
    
    Driver->>PCI: pci_enable_device(), pci_request_regions()
    Driver->>PCI: pci_ioremap_bar(pdev, 0)
    PCI-->>Driver: Returns mmio_base (Virtual Addr mapped to BAR0)
    
    Driver->>PCI: pci_alloc_irq_vectors() (Request MSI Vector 0)
    Driver->>PCI: request_irq(dev->irq, vgpu_irq_handler)
    
    Driver->>RAM: dma_alloc_coherent() (Allocate Ring Buffer 4KB)
    RAM-->>Driver: Return Virtual Addr (CPU) & Bus Addr (FPGA dma_handle)
    Note over Driver, Regs: Provide FPGA with Ring Buffer Base Address (64-bit split)
    Driver->>PCIe: iowrite32(lower_32_bits(dma_handle), mmio_base + 0x0C)
    Driver->>PCIe: iowrite32(upper_32_bits(dma_handle), mmio_base + 0x10)
    PCIe->>SmartConnect: Route AXI-Lite Write to vgpu_top
    SmartConnect->>Regs: Latch reg_ring_dma_addr [63:0]
    
    Note over Driver, Regs: Provide FPGA with UVM Mode & Page Table Base Address
    Driver->>PCIe: iowrite32(uvm_mode, mmio_base + 0x20)
    PCIe->>SmartConnect: Route AXI-Lite Write
    SmartConnect->>Regs: Latch reg_uvm_mode (0 = Direct/IOMMU, 1 = Scatter-Gather)

    alt uvm_mode == 1 (Scatter-Gather)
        Driver->>RAM: dma_alloc_coherent() (Allocate Software Page Table 64KB)
        Driver->>PCIe: iowrite32(lower_32_bits(page_table_dma), mmio_base + 0x14)
        Driver->>PCIe: iowrite32(upper_32_bits(page_table_dma), mmio_base + 0x18)
        PCIe->>SmartConnect: Route AXI-Lite Write
        SmartConnect->>Regs: Latch reg_pagetable_dma_addr [63:0]
    end
    
    Driver->>VFS: cdev_add(), device_create(/dev/vgpu0)

    %% Phase 2: User Initialization
    Note over App, Core: [Phase 2] Application Initialization
    App->>VFS: open("/dev/vgpu0")
    VFS->>Driver: vgpu_open() (Allocates vgpu_context)
    Driver-->>App: File Descriptor (fd)
    
    App->>VFS: mmap(fd, size=4096, offset=0)
    VFS->>Driver: vgpu_mmap(pgoff=0)
    Driver->>Driver: dma_mmap_coherent() (Map Ring Buffer to User Virtual Addr)
    Driver-->>App: Return Ring Buffer Virtual Address (ring_ptr)
    
    App->>RAM: malloc(payload_size) (User Space Memory Allocation)
    Note over App: CPU Page Faults occur when App writes to malloc memory (Demand Paging!)

    %% Phase 3: Command Submission & Doorbell (PCIe + AXI)
    Note over App, Core: [Phase 3] Command Submission & Doorbell Trigger
    
    App->>VFS: ioctl(fd, VGPU_IOC_SUBMIT_CMD, &user_cmd)
    VFS->>Driver: vgpu_ioctl()
    Note over Driver, RAM: Unified Memory Setup (Demand Paging)
    Driver->>RAM: get_user_pages_fast(user_vaddr) (Lock/Pin User Pages)
    
    alt uvm_mode == 0 (IOMMU Contiguous)
        Driver->>Driver: dma_map_sg() (Request IOMMU to coalesce pages into single IOVA)
        Driver->>PCIe: iowrite32(lower_32_bits(contiguous_iova), mmio_base + 0x14)
        Driver->>PCIe: iowrite32(upper_32_bits(contiguous_iova), mmio_base + 0x18)
        PCIe->>SmartConnect: Route AXI-Lite Write
        SmartConnect->>Regs: Latch contiguous payload address into reg_pagetable_dma_addr
    else uvm_mode == 1 (Scatter-Gather)
        Driver->>Driver: dma_map_page() (Map each pinned page to DMA address)
        Driver->>RAM: Write mapped DMA physical addresses into dev->page_table[]
    end
    
    Driver->>RAM: Write Command Data to ring->cmds[tail] (16 Bytes: opcode, size, vaddr)
    Note over Driver: CPU Producer: Update Tail with Memory Barrier
    Driver->>RAM: smp_store_release(&ring->tail) (Ensure command committed before tail updates!)
    Driver-->>App: VGPU_IOC_SUBMIT_CMD returns
    
    App->>VFS: ioctl(fd, VGPU_IOC_DOORBELL)
    VFS->>Driver: vgpu_ioctl()
    
    Note over Driver: Clear irq_fired = 0 (Prevent Lost Wakeup)
    
    Note over Driver, PCIe: iowrite32(1, mmio_base + 0x00)
    Driver->>PCIe: Issue Memory Write TLP (Target: BAR0 + 0x00 - Doorbell)
    Driver->>Driver: wait_event_interruptible(&dev->wait_q)
    Note over App, Driver: Thread goes to SLEEP (Context Switch)

    PCIe->>AXI_PCIe: Deliver TLP to FPGA Endpoint
    AXI_PCIe->>SmartConnect: AXI-Lite Write (Addr: 0x00, Data: 1)
    SmartConnect->>Regs: Pulse doorbell_pulse = 1
    Regs->>DMA: Trigger start_doorbell (DMA FSM exits S_IDLE)

    %% Phase 4: FPGA DMA & Streaming Execution
    Note over App, Core: [Phase 4] AXI4-Full Command Fetch & Streaming Compute
    
    Note over DMA, PCIe: FPGA Consumer: Read Command Packet
    DMA->>AXI_PCIe: AXI Read: ring_base_addr + 8 + head*16 (arlen=1, 2 beats = 16B)
    AXI_PCIe->>RAM: PCIe Memory Read TLP (Host RAM)
    RAM-->>AXI_PCIe: Return 128-bit Command Struct
    AXI_PCIe-->>DMA: Beat 0: opcode [31:0] + payload_size [63:32]
    Note over DMA: Calculate dynamic payload_burst_len = ceil(size / 8) - 1
    AXI_PCIe-->>DMA: Beat 1: payload_vaddr [63:0]
    
    alt uvm_mode == 1 (Scatter-Gather Page Table)
        Note over DMA, AXI_PCIe: Page Table Walk (Fetch Physical Page Pointer)
        DMA->>AXI_PCIe: AXI Read: pt_base_addr + (VPN * 8) (arlen=0, 8B)
        AXI_PCIe->>RAM: PCIe Memory Read TLP (Page Table Entry)
        RAM-->>AXI_PCIe: Return 64-bit Physical Page DMA Address
        AXI_PCIe-->>DMA: m_axi_rdata (Physical Page Base)
        Note over DMA: Calculate final_payload_addr = Page Base + Page Offset [11:0]
    else uvm_mode == 0 (IOMMU Contiguous)
        Note over DMA: Set final_payload_addr = pt_base_addr
    end

    Note over DMA, Core: Streaming Burst Read & Vector SIMD ALU Pipeline
    DMA->>AXI_PCIe: AXI Read Burst: final_payload_addr (arlen = payload_burst_len)
    AXI_PCIe->>RAM: PCIe Memory Read TLP (Payload Data)
    
    loop Streaming Read & SIMD Vector Compute (Wire Speed)
        RAM-->>AXI_PCIe: Payload Data Stream (64-bit / clock)
        AXI_PCIe-->>DMA: m_axi_rdata (64-bit chunk)
        DMA->>Core: compute_in_buf <= m_axi_rdata, valid_in <= 1
        Core->>Core: 1-Cycle SIMD ALU: Vector Add (+1) / Mul (*2)
        Core-->>DMA: compute_out_buf, valid_out <= 1
        Note over DMA: Stream Buffer (2KB on-chip BRAM) captures computed results (wire speed)
    end

    %% Phase 5: In-Place Result Writeback
    Note over App, Core: [Phase 5] In-Place Result Writeback & Head Update
    DMA->>AXI_PCIe: AXI Write Burst: final_payload_addr (awlen = payload_burst_len)
    loop Streaming Burst Writeback
        Note over DMA: Stream computed results out of 2KB BRAM (stream_buf[i])
        DMA->>AXI_PCIe: m_axi_wdata <= stream_buf[i], wstrb = 0xFF
        AXI_PCIe->>RAM: PCIe Memory Write TLP (Computed Results In-Place)
    end
    AXI_PCIe-->>DMA: m_axi_bvalid (Write Response OK)
    
    Note over DMA, RAM: FPGA Consumer: Update Head Pointer
    DMA->>AXI_PCIe: AXI Write: ring_base_addr (Offset: 0x00, awlen=0, wstrb=0x0F)
    Note over DMA: Write new head pointer (Protected WSTRB prevents tail corruption!)
    AXI_PCIe->>RAM: PCIe Memory Write TLP (Update ring->head)
    AXI_PCIe-->>DMA: m_axi_bvalid (Write Response OK)

    %% Phase 6: Interrupt & Wakeup
    Note over App, Core: [Phase 6] MSI Interrupt & Thread Wakeup
    DMA->>Regs: Assert task_done_irq = 1
    Regs->>AXI_PCIe: Assert usr_irq_req / INTX_MSI_Request
    AXI_PCIe->>PCIe: Issue MSI Memory Write TLP (Vector 0 to CPU APIC)
    
    PCIe->>PCI: CPU receives MSI Interrupt
    PCI->>Driver: Execute Top-Half: vgpu_irq_handler()
    
    Note over Driver, Regs: Acknowledge Hardware Interrupt
    Driver->>PCIe: ioread32(mmio_base + 0x04) (Read INT_STATUS)
    PCIe->>SmartConnect: AXI-Lite Read
    SmartConnect->>Regs: Read int_status_reg (bit 0 = 1)
    
    Driver->>PCIe: iowrite32(1, mmio_base + 0x08) (Write INT_ACK)
    PCIe->>SmartConnect: AXI-Lite Write
    SmartConnect->>Regs: Clear int_status_reg bit 0
    
    Note over Driver: Wake up Application
    Driver->>Driver: dev->irq_fired = 1, wake_up_interruptible(&dev->wait_q)
    Driver-->>PCI: return IRQ_HANDLED (Exit Interrupt Context)
    
    Note over Driver: Wakes up from wait_event_interruptible
    Note over Driver, RAM: Unified Memory Teardown
    alt uvm_mode == 0
        Driver->>Driver: dma_unmap_sg() (Unmap IOVA)
    else uvm_mode == 1
        Driver->>Driver: dma_unmap_page() (Unmap Scatter-Gather Pages)
    end
    Driver->>RAM: put_page() (Unpin/Release physical pages)
    
    Driver-->>App: ioctl(VGPU_IOC_DOORBELL) returns SUCCESS!
    Note over App: Thread WAKES UP. Results are ready in memory!
